solution_md:
Call all such numbersthat can be expressed by the sum of a red integer and a blue integer *good*. Let  $\mathbb{P}*$  denote the probability that a number,  $i$ , is [i]good*. By Linearity of Expectation, the expected value is
\begin{align*}
\sum_{i=3}^{19}\mathbb{P}[i]=\frac{1}{2}+\frac{1}{2}+\frac{3}{4}+\frac{3}{4}+\frac{7}{8}+\frac{7}{8}+\frac{15}{16}+\frac{15}{16}+\frac{31}{32}+\frac{15}{16}+\frac{15}{16}+\frac{7}{8}+\frac{7}{8}+\frac{3}{4}+\frac{3}{4}+\frac{1}{2}+\frac{1}{2}=\frac{423}{32}.
\end{align*}
The requested sum is  $423+32=455$ .

