solution_md:
Let  $a\to b$  denote that there exists a directed path from  $a$  to  $b$ . Label the rightmost three vertices  $1,\,2,\,3$  from bottom to top. Let  $x_n$  denote the number of orientations of a  $3\times n$  grid with property  $x$ , where  $x$  is to be replaced with the following letters:
\begin{align*}
a&:(1\to 2)(2\to 3)
b&:(2\to 1)(3\to 2)
c&:(1\to 2)(3\to 2)
d&:(1\to 2)(3\to 2)(1\to 3)
e&:(1\to 2)(3\to 2)(3\to 1)
f&:(2\to 1)(2\to 3)
g&:(2\to 1)(2\to 3)(1\to 3)
h&:(2\to 1)(2\to 3)(3\to 1).
\end{align*}
We have the following system of recurrence relations:
\begin{align*}
a_n&=8a_{n-1}+4b_{n-1}+6c_{n-1}+6d_{n-1}+5e_{n-1}+6f_{n-1}+6g_{n-1}+5h_{n-1}
b_n&=4a_{n-1}+8b_{n-1}+6c_{n-1}+5d_{n-1}+6e_{n-1}+6f_{n-1}+5g_{n-1}+6h_{n-1}
c_n&=5a_{n-1}+5b_{n-1}+8c_{n-1}+6d_{n-1}+6e_{n-1}+5f_{n-1}+4g_{n-1}+4h_{n-1}
d_n&=1a_{n-1}+0b_{n-1}+0c_{n-1}+2d_{n-1}+0e_{n-1}+0f_{n-1}+1g_{n-1}+0h_{n-1}
e_n&=0a_{n-1}+1b_{n-1}+0c_{n-1}+0d_{n-1}+2e_{n-1}+0f_{n-1}+0g_{n-1}+1h_{n-1}
f_n&=5a_{n-1}+5b_{n-1}+5c_{n-1}+4d_{n-1}+4e_{n-1}+8f_{n-1}+6g_{n-1}+6h_{n-1}
g_n&=1a_{n-1}+0b_{n-1}+0c_{n-1}+1d_{n-1}+0e_{n-1}+0f_{n-1}+2g_{n-1}+0h_{n-1}
h_n&=0a_{n-1}+1b_{n-1}+0c_{n-1}+0d_{n-1}+1e_{n-1}+0f_{n-1}+0g_{n-1}+2h_{n-1}.
\end{align*}
Letting  $x_n:=a_n+b_n$ ,  $y_n:=c_n+f_n$ , and  $z_n:=d_n+e_n+g_n+h_n$ , we get
\begin{align*}
x_n&=12x_{n-1}+12y_{n-1}+11z_{n-1}
y_n&=10x_{n-1}+13y_{n-1}+10z_{n-1}
z_n&=2x_{n-1}+3z_{n-1}.
\end{align*}
Note that  $a_1=b_1=c_1=f_1=1$  and  $d_1=e_1=g_1=h_1=0$  so  $x_1=y_1=2$  and  $z_1=0$ . Thus we need to calculate
\[
\begin{pmatrix}
x_{2025}
y_{2025}
z_{2025}
\end{pmatrix}
=
\begin{pmatrix}
12 & 12 & 11
10 & 13 & 10
2 & 0 & 3
\end{pmatrix}^{2024}
\begin{pmatrix}
2
2
0
\end{pmatrix}.
\]
Let  $A$  be the matrix. Note that the characteristic polynomial of  $A$  is  $x^3-28x^2+89x-61=0$ , which has roots  $1,\,\frac{27\pm\sqrt{481}}{2}$ .

The eigenvalues of  $A$  as a  $\mathbb{F}_5$ -matrix are  $1,\,3,\,4$ . Hence there exists an invertible matrix  $P$  such that the diagonal of  $PAP^{-1}$  is  $1,\,3,\,4$  in some order, and everywhere else the matrix is  $0$ . Note that then  $(PAP^{-1})^4=I$  so  $A^4=I$ . Thus  $A^{2024}=I$  over  $\mathbb{F}_5$ . It follows that  $x_{2025}+y_{2025}+z_{2025}\equiv 4\pmod{5}$ .

Now let us work in  $\mathbb{F}_{499}$ . Note that  $481=201^2$ . Hence the eigenvalues of  $A$  are  $1,\,114,\,412$ . Similarly,  $A^{498}=I$  so  $A^{2024}=A^{32}$ . Computation gives
\[
A^{32}=
\begin{pmatrix}
409 & 136 & 408
181 & 296 & 181
454 & 181 & 455
\end{pmatrix}.
\]
It follows that  $x_{2025}+y_{2025}+z_{2025}\equiv 2(409+136+181+296+454+181)\equiv 320\pmod{499}$ .

